<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    The contract the platform reads before it will treat this app as a digital
    assistant at all. VoiceInteractionServiceInfo parses this resource and answers
    with a reason for every field it cannot find, so the whole voice-interaction
    path - the system "Default digital assistant" picker, onReady(), showSession()
    - is dead while any of it is missing.

    The fields are attributes of this element, not child elements: the parser reads
    them through getAttribute (sessionService, recognitionService, settingsActivity,
    supportsAssist, ...) and a parse error sets mValid = false in
    VoiceInteractionManagerServiceImpl, which means onReady() never runs and
    showSession() throws.

    sessionService and recognitionService are both required - the parser reports
    "No sessionService specified" and "No recognitionService specified" - and both
    are resolved in this app's own package, so they are dotted class names relative
    to it.

    settingsActivity is the activity the platform opens when the user wants to
    configure the assistant; MainActivity is the app's only entry point.

    supportsLocalInteraction is what the platform needs to know to host the
    exchange on the device itself rather than remotely, which is the whole point
    of a local-first assistant.

    supportsLaunchVoiceAssistFromKeyguard defaults to false in the parser too, so
    it has to be stated for the assistant to be reachable from the lock screen -
    the one place the exchange is drawn where none of this app's own windows exist.
-->
<voice-interaction-service
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:sessionService="com.localassistant.app.service.WakeChatSessionService"
    android:recognitionService="com.localassistant.app.service.WakeChatRecognitionService"
    android:settingsActivity="com.localassistant.app.ui.MainActivity"
    android:supportsAssist="true"
    android:supportsLaunchVoiceAssistFromKeyguard="true"
    android:supportsLocalInteraction="true" />
